    <PackageReleaseNotes>- Created `ExceptionExtensions`
  - Just a helper inside that sets the current stacktrace
- `Slug&lt;TFormatter&gt;` now implements `IComparable&lt;Slug&lt;TFormatter&gt;&gt;` and `IComparable`
- Created `IResultState`, a common class between all Result types
- Implemented conversion operators and helper methods for conversion between Result types
  - For most Result types, you can now directly return either an exception or the success value without a wrapper ctor call.
- Added `BooleanResult.Successful` and `TransportableBooleanResult.Successful` to avoid an extra ctor call

- Created `TypeRegistry`
  - Acts mostly like a cache for types, fetching new types on read
  - The registry part comes from the fact that you need a validator to 'register' types
    - This validator gets all the needed metadata and verifies that the type can be used in a given `TypeRegistry`
- Created `GlobalTypeRegistry`
  - Like `TypeRegistry`, but does the actual caching.
- Created `ITypeRegistryValidator`
  - Intended to take a type and verify that it can be used in a `TypeRegistry` with this validator
  - Also gets the key for the type
- Created `SingletonTypeRegistry`
  - A lazy singleton `TypeRegistry`

- Fixed `Dirtifier.Set`
- Created IProvider
  - Simple interfaces for providing an object with the given args and verification
- Created ISingleton
  - Simple interface for defining a singleton instance

### Breaking Changes
- Removed BiDictionary
  - Another BiDictionary implementation already exists on NuGet, it's not worth trying to upkeep this.

- Due to the new `IResultState`, all result classes has `Success` renamed to `IsSuccessful`
- Due to the new `IResultState`, `IBooleanResult` was removed</PackageReleaseNotes>
